      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.751,
            0.063,
            0.834,
            0.08
          ],
          "content": "Fractions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.118,
            0.472,
            0.15
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, ${ \\frac { 2 } { 3 } } \\quad + \\quad { \\frac { 1 } { 5 } } \\quad = \\quad { \\frac { 1 0 } { 1 5 } } \\quad + \\quad { \\frac { 3 } { 1 5 } } \\quad = \\quad { \\frac { 1 3 } { 1 5 } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.166,
            0.491,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": "**Example**: Find the sum of $\\frac{1}{6}$ and $\\frac { 1 } { 3 }$ ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.195,
            0.601,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": "The smallest common multiple of 6 and 3 is 6."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.22,
            0.302,
            0.248
          ],
          "content": "$\\frac{1}{6}$ will remain $\\frac{1}{6}$ ."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.249,
            0.253,
            0.279
          ],
          "content": "{ \\frac { 1 } { 3 } } = { \\frac { 1 \\times 2 } { 3 \\times 2 } }   =   { \\frac { 2 } { 6 } }",
          "image_source": "images/page_28_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.283,
            0.429,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, ${ \\frac { 1 } { 6 } } + { \\frac { 1 } { 3 } } = { \\frac { 1 } { 6 } } + { \\frac { 2 } { 6 } } = { \\frac { 3 } { 6 } } .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.324,
            0.836,
            0.398
          ],
          "content": "The fraction $\\frac{3}{6}$ can now be re-expressed in lowest terms, if desired. This can be done by dividing both the numerator and denominator by 3 (the biggest common factor of 3 and 6):"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.406,
            0.253,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": "36 3 6 ÷ 3 3 12 = ÷ = ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.453,
            0.355,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, ${ \\frac { 1 } { 6 } } \\quad + \\quad { \\frac { 1 } { 3 } } \\quad = \\quad { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.498,
            0.145,
            0.521
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_28_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
